## 11. Edge Cases

### Add Expense
- Empty description
- Description containing only spaces
- Amount is 0
- Negative amount
- Non-numeric amount
- Missing amount
- Missing category
- Invalid category
- Invalid date
- Missing date

### Read Expenses
- No expenses exist
- Invalid category filter
- No expenses match the selected category
- Backend/database unavailable

### Update Expense
- Invalid expense ID
- Expense ID does not exist
- Invalid updated amount
- Invalid updated category
- Empty updated description

### Delete Expense
- Invalid expense ID
- Expense does not exist
- Database unavailable

### Frontend
- API request fails
- Loading state
- Empty expense list
- Server returns an error

---

## 12. Validation Rules

Validation must happen on the backend even if the frontend also validates input.

The backend should reject:

```text
description = ""
description = "   "
amount <= 0
amount = non-numeric value
category = invalid category
invalid date
```

The frontend should provide useful feedback before or after submitting invalid data.

